  "summary": "This pass repairs what the same-family trail review of S2 to S5 found. The S5 evaluator also requires both arms to share one preflight reference, so a candidate that renders different text everywhere fails correctness. A failed latest run shows its failure stage instead of older values. Admission reads recorded inputs only from sourceIdentity.measuredInputs and computes states from reason codes. Threshold rows use the comparison operator the clipboard producer now records. Registry validation allows evidence on one artifact per target and recipe variables only before the first word. The issue #6038 workload drops its non-equivalent stand-in. writeBenchmarkResult sets strictValidation for eight producers. The evaluator and external-text tests run in the fast suite. The core-node-transforms guard exposed a Plite regression in tx.nodes.wrap with a root path and a selector, which the public binding fix and a transforms contract test close; the unwrap lane now checks its setup.",
