    "limits": "Browser and CLI runtime proofs live in scratch and are described in the plan. On three production builds of snapshot d96ecb4f55bd82a0: 8 functional spec tests pass on the baseline; a 12-cell preflight sweep passes on the baseline and a slower candidate; a candidate that drops the last parsed block fails only on the shared reference and passes without that rule; the slower candidate fails latency. A source-matched native code-block run passes validity and misses native budgets, which stays inconclusive without a matched baseline. A strict schema-construction run replaced a hand-written passing stub; the other seven producers rely on the helper tests. core-node-transforms and collab-readiness reran current. Not claimed: performance acceptance, calibration of the 1.20 attribution guard, all-target reruns. 17 of 20 lab artifacts stay unknown because their producers record no inputs, and tracked generated outputs reflect this host. check:plite:contracts fails on three test-suite-routing cases and the clipboard live-encode test, all failing identically at HEAD. The ledger inventory is stale in four groups that mix this plan with other sessions, pending the user refresh."
